version: 1.0.0
description: Canvas 2D renderer — transforms resolved frame data into visual output via Canvas API
context:
  - This package renders resolved animation frames to Canvas 2D contexts
  - Uses a minimal RenderContext interface to avoid DOM lib dependency
  - Supports shape (rect, ellipse, path), text, image (with sourceRect/spritesheet crop), video, and group layers
  - Image renderer supports 5-arg and 9-arg drawImage for sourceRect cropping and spritesheet grid rendering
  - 'Video renderer uses injected VideoFrameProvider (preview: HTMLVideoElement, export: WebCodecs/Mediabunny)'
  - Tint compositing via offscreen canvas (multiply blend + destination-in alpha mask)
  - EffectiveLayer includes visible, tint, and animated image properties
  - Transform stack handles translate, rotate, scale with anchor points
  - Percentage units resolved to pixels at render time
components:
  render-frame:
    description: Main entry — clears canvas, iterates layers (painters algorithm), applies transform stack, dispatches to renderers; tracks videoSourceTime per layer
    components:
      - '#frame-resolver'
      - '#apply-properties'
      - '#shape-renderer'
      - '#text-renderer'
      - '#video-renderer'
    file: src/render-frame.ts
  shape-renderer:
    description: Renders rect (with cornerRadius/roundRect), ellipse, and path (with bezier curves) shapes; includes perimeter calculations for stroke trim
    file: src/renderers/shape-renderer.ts
  text-renderer:
    description: Renders text layers with font building, fill color, and alignment
    file: src/renderers/text-renderer.ts
  video-renderer:
    description: Renders video layers via injected VideoFrameProvider — returns without drawing if provider returns null (caller retries)
    tags:
      - video
      - renderer
    file: src/renderers/video-renderer.ts
  apply-properties:
    description: Merges computed animation properties over layer defaults, resolves percentage units to pixels
    file: src/apply-properties.ts
  canvas-styles:
    description: colorToCSS conversion, applyFill (solid/linear/radial gradient), applyStroke with dash and strokeStart/strokeEnd trim support
    file: src/styles.ts
aspects:
  painters-algorithm-order:
    description: Layers render in effList order — first element is drawn first and ends up at the back, last on top. The list is built by iterating resolvedFrame.layers in order, so resolution order IS z-order. There is no separate sort or z-index.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - ordering
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:56-66
    enforcement: iterate effList in resolution order
  save-restore-per-layer:
    description: Each layer is wrapped in a single ctx.save()/ctx.restore() pair, so all transform-stack, globalAlpha, blend-mode, shadow, and clip mutations are scoped to that layer and never leak into the next. Skip the restore and every subsequent layer inherits stale transforms.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - transform
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:91-92
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:213
    enforcement: balanced save/restore per layer
  transform-stack-anchor-order:
    description: Transform order is translate(x,y) → translate(+anchorPixel) → rotate → scale → translate(-anchorPixel), so rotation and scale pivot around the anchor point (anchorX*width, anchorY*height) rather than the layer origin. Rotation combines explicit rotation + motionPathAngle, and the rotate/scale block is skipped entirely when both are identity.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - transform
      - ordering
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:104-122
    enforcement: anchor translate around rotate/scale
  ancestor-transforms-root-first:
    description: applyAncestorTransforms walks the parentId chain collecting ancestors child→root, then applies them in REVERSE (root first, direct parent last) so child layers inherit the composed parent transform. A visited Set guards against circular parentId references looping forever.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - transform
      - edge-case
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:285-319
    enforcement: reverse-apply chain + visited-set guard
  tint-offscreen-multiply-mask:
    description: 'Tint is only applied when ctx.createOffscreen exists and tint.amount > 0. The technique: render content to an offscreen canvas, multiply-fill the tint color over it, then destination-in re-render of the content as an alpha mask so the tint only colors opaque pixels; finally the original is drawn and the tinted offscreen overlaid at globalAlpha = tint.amount. Content is re-rendered up to three times.'
    tags:
      - compositing
      - technique
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:137-211
    enforcement: offscreen multiply + destination-in mask
  early-skip-invisible-layers:
    description: A layer is skipped before any save/transform when eff.visible is false OR eff.opacity <= 0, so fully hidden/transparent layers cost nothing and emit no canvas state. image layers only render when an imageCache is supplied and video layers only when a videoFrameProvider is supplied.
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - performance
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:69-73
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:158-165
    enforcement: guard clauses before save
  render-context-no-dom-dependency:
    description: Renderers type their context as the local RenderContext interface (canvas-types.ts), never DOM lib CanvasRenderingContext2D, so the canvas package compiles and runs without a DOM lib — the same code drives browser canvas, OffscreenCanvas, and node/export backends. drawImage sources are passed as unknown to bridge the typing gap.
    tags:
      - architecture
      - core-invariant
      - portability
    anchors:
      - src/renderers/video-renderer.ts:2-2
      - src/renderers/video-renderer.ts:24-24
    enforcement: depend on RenderContext interface only
  perimeter-from-shape-type:
    description: Stroke trim (strokeStart/strokeEnd dash math) needs a path length, so each shape computes its own perimeter — rect via 2*(w+h), ellipse via the Ramanujan approximation, path by summing segment chord distances with bezier segments fudged at chord * 1.2. Wrong perimeter desyncs the dash offset and the trim animation drifts.
    tags:
      - approximation
      - magic-number
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/renderers/shape-renderer.ts:26-64
    enforcement: per-shape perimeter formula
  rounded-rect-feature-detect:
    description: roundRect is feature-detected (cornerRadius && ctx.roundRect) — when a cornerRadius is set but the context lacks roundRect, rect rendering falls back to plain fillRect/strokeRect (square corners) rather than throwing. clipPath has its own manual moveTo/lineTo fallback for the same reason.
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - feature-detection
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/renderers/shape-renderer.ts:77-94
      - packages/canvas/src/render-frame.ts:222-231
    enforcement: feature-detect roundRect with fallback
  path-needs-two-points:
    description: renderPath returns immediately if fewer than 2 points, and a segment is drawn as a bezierCurveTo only when the previous point has an out handle AND the current point has an in handle — otherwise it degrades to a straight lineTo. Handle coordinates are relative offsets added to the anchor point.
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - geometry
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/renderers/shape-renderer.ts:124-144
    enforcement: guard length + handle-pair check
  text-align-offset-baseline:
    description: Canvas textAlign anchors at the draw point, so the X draw position is offset to keep text inside the layer bounds — left=0, center=width/2, right=width. textBaseline is forced to "top" so y=0 is the top edge of the box, matching the layer coordinate system rather than the canvas alphabetic default.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - text
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/renderers/text-renderer.ts:17-36
    enforcement: align-derived X offset + top baseline
  font-string-assembly:
    description: The CSS font shorthand is assembled in strict order "<fontStyle> <fontWeight> <fontSizepx> <fontFamily>" with fontStyle/fontWeight defaulting to "normal"; fontSize is always emitted in px. Reorder the tokens and the canvas silently ignores the malformed font string.
    tags:
      - text
      - gotcha
      - ordering
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/renderers/text-renderer.ts:11-15
    enforcement: fixed CSS font token order
  video-null-provider-retry:
    description: renderVideo draws nothing (silent return) when visual.src is missing OR the provider returns null — null means the frame is not decoded yet, and the contract is that the caller re-renders on a later tick until the provider yields a frame. No placeholder is drawn, so the previous frame content remains visible.
    anchors:
      - src/renderers/video-renderer.ts:18-30
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - video
      - async
    enforcement: silent return on null frame
  effective-property-override-defaults:
    description: buildEffectiveLayer merges computedProperties (animated values) over layer defaults using ?? chains — cp value first, then the static layer field, then a hard default. shadow and tint blocks are only constructed when either the static layer has them OR a relevant computed key is present, otherwise they stay undefined to skip that work downstream.
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - merge
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/apply-properties.ts:72-117
    enforcement: cp ?? layer ?? default chain
  percentage-resolved-at-render:
    description: resolveUnit converts a percentage string to pixels (parseFloat/100 * reference) at render time, with x/width measured against parentWidth and y/height against parentHeight. Raw numbers pass through unchanged. The correct reference axis must be supplied per field — using the wrong dimension skews percentage layouts.
    tags:
      - units
      - convention
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/apply-properties.ts:51-56
      - packages/canvas/src/apply-properties.ts:76-97
    enforcement: percent detect + per-axis reference
  visual-override-copy-on-write:
    description: buildEffectiveVisual returns the ORIGINAL visual untouched when no visual/image computed keys are present, and otherwise shallow-clones before mutating fill/stroke/style/sourceRect — so the source document visual is never mutated. frameIndex is floored to an integer when animated.
    tags:
      - immutability
      - merge
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/apply-properties.ts:124-146
      - packages/canvas/src/apply-properties.ts:234-236
    enforcement: early-return original else clone
  stroke-trim-via-dash:
    description: strokeStart/strokeEnd trim is implemented with the line-dash trick — a dash of [visible, pathLength+1] plus lineDashOffset = -start*pathLength reveals only the (end-start)*pathLength segment of the perimeter. The +1 guarantees the gap exceeds the path so only one dash shows; visible is clamped to >= 0. Plain stroke.dash applies only when no trim is set.
    tags:
      - technique
      - magic-number
      - stroke
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/styles.ts:73-82
    enforcement: dash array + dash offset trim
  color-css-type-dispatch:
    description: 'colorToCSS dispatches on shape — a string passes through as a hex literal, an object with "r" becomes rgba() with r/g/b rounded, an object with "h" becomes hsla(); anything else falls back to #000000. The fallback means malformed color objects render black rather than throwing.'
    tags:
      - dispatch
      - edge-case
      - color
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/styles.ts:7-21
    enforcement: shape-based dispatch + black fallback
  gradient-geometry-from-bounds:
    description: applyFill builds gradients from the layer bounds — a linear gradient spans the box along the fill.angle (centered, ±cos/sin * half-extent), and a radial gradient resolves percentage center/radius against width/height (radius against max(width,height)). Gradient coordinates are local to the layer, so they animate correctly under the transform stack.
    tags:
      - geometry
      - gradient
      - units
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/styles.ts:32-59
    enforcement: bounds-derived gradient coordinates
